  "id": "Compound::DB01576 - Gene::147",
  "verbalization": "Dextroamphetamine is implicated in the interaction with Adra1b through multiple pathways that converge on the central nervous system and organonitrogen compound classes. The evidence suggests that Dextroamphetamine binds to Adra1a, which in turn participates in alpha-adrenergic receptor activity, ultimately involving Adra1b. Additionally, Dextroamphetamine is included in the class of central nervous system stimulants, which includes Lisdexamfetamine, a compound that binds to Adra1b. This indicates a potential mechanism where Dextroamphetamine, through its inclusion in a broader class of stimulants, indirectly influences Adra1b via Lisdexamfetamine. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on the central nervous system and organonitrogen compound classes, suggesting that Dextroamphetamine may exert its effects on Adra1b through a chain of interactions that involve both direct and indirect mechanisms.",
